{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityFromSelfDuality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityFromSelfDuality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.SymplecticGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.commute_diagMat_imp_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.commute_diagMat_imp_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L256-L286","doc":"**Maximality ingredient — a regular torus element centralizes only diagonals.**\nIf a `2×2` matrix `M` commutes with `diag(t, t⁻¹)` for a **regular** unit `t`\n(`t² ≠ 1` — which needs the base ring to carry a unit of order `> 2`, true for\nthe archimedean substrate `ℝ`/`ℂ`, false over `𝔽₂`/`𝔽₃`), then `M` is\n**diagonal** (`M 0 1 = M 1 0 = 0`). Proof: the `(0,1)`/`(1,0)` entries of\n`M·diag = diag·M` force `M 0 1·(1 − t²) = 0` and likewise for `M 1 0`, and\n`1 − t² ≠ 0` in a field.\n\nConsequence: the centralizer of a regular element of the diagonal torus is\ncontained in the diagonals, so (with `sl2_diagonal_eq_diagEmbed`) the diagonal\n`𝔾ₘ` is **self-centralizing** — the standard criterion for a *maximal* torus in\na connected reductive group. This is a genuine ingredient of the maximality\nstep (rank ≤ 1); concluding rank ≤ 1 from it still needs the connected-reductive\nstructure theory, so it does **not** by itself close the atomicity upper bound\n(bean `qou-atsd-t3`). The `t² ≠ 1` hypothesis honestly records that maximality\nrequires the substrate's ring-richness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sl2_diagonal_eq_diagEmbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sl2_diagonal_eq_diagEmbed","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L221-L245","doc":"**T3, `m = 1`, the diagonal torus is EXACTLY `𝔾ₘ` (the torus-level upper\nbound).** A *diagonal* matrix in `SL₂(R)` (off-diagonal entries zero) is\n`diag(t, t⁻¹)` for a unit `t`: from `det = a·d = 1`, `a` is a unit with inverse\n`d`. So the diagonal torus is *precisely* the range of `diagEmbedHom` — a single\n`𝔾ₘ`, **rank exactly 1** (both bounds, for this torus): it cannot be larger.\n\nThis closes the torus-level upper bound. The remaining atomicity gap is\nstrictly the *maximality* step — that no larger torus lives elsewhere in `SL₂`\n(all maximal tori conjugate) — which is the root-count fact (bean\n`qou-atsd-t3`, upper). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.diagEmbedHom_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.diagEmbedHom_injective","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L199-L219","doc":"**T3, `m = 1`, the LOWER bound (`rank SL₂ ≥ 1`).** The diagonal torus\nembedding `diagEmbedHom : Rˣ →* SL₂(R)`, `t ↦ diag(t, t⁻¹)`, is **injective**\n(read `s = t` off the `(0,0)` entry). So `SL₂(R)` contains a *faithful* copy of\nthe unit group `Rˣ = 𝔾ₘ` as its diagonal torus — the maximal-torus *candidate*\nis realised, giving `rank SL₂ ≥ 1`.\n\n**Honest scope (critical-distance correction).** This is the **lower** bound.\nThe atomicity chain needs `rank G ≤ rank Sp(V) ≤ 1`, i.e. the **upper** bound\n`rank SL₂ ≤ 1` — that this `𝔾ₘ` is *maximal*, that `SL₂` contains **no**\ntwo-parameter torus. That upper direction (the root-count / \"no larger torus\"\nfact) is the genuinely hard part and remains **open** (bean `qou-atsd-t3`,\nupper). This lemma builds the torus the maximality argument is *about*; it does\n**not** by itself establish the atomicity bound. Combined with `Sp₂ = SL₂`\n(`sp2_mem_iff_det_one`) it fixes the dimension-2 anchor's torus, one honest\nbrick short of `rank G ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.diagEmbedHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.diagEmbedHom","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L192-L197","doc":"**The diagonal torus embedding** `Rˣ → SL₂(R)`, `t ↦ diag(t, t⁻¹)`, as a group\nhomomorphism (`diag` is multiplicative and unital). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.diagMat_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.diagMat_mul","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L187-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.diagMat_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.diagMat_one","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L184-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.diagMat_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.diagMat_det","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L180-L182","doc":"`det diag(t, t⁻¹) = t · t⁻¹ = 1`, so the diagonal matrix lies in `SL₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.diagMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.diagMat","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L176-L178","doc":"The diagonal matrix `diag(t, t⁻¹)` for a unit `t` — a point of the SL₂\nmaximal torus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.sp2_mem_iff_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.sp2_mem_iff_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L149-L165","doc":"**`Sp₂ = SL₂` (matrix level, `det = +1`).** A 2×2 matrix preserves the\nsymplectic form `J₂` **iff** its determinant is `1`. This is the sharp dim-2\naccident that upgrades `symplectic_det_sq_eq_one` (`det² = 1`, all dimensions)\nto `det = +1` in dimension 2 — the base case (`m = 1`) of the classical\n`rank Sp(2m) = m` residual (T3): `Sp₂ = SL₂`, a rank-1 group.\n\n(Mathlib's `symplecticGroup (Fin 1) R` uses the `Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 1` index; the\ncorrespondence to this `Fin 2` form is a reindex — bean `qou-atsd-t1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.mul_J2_mul_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.mul_J2_mul_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L138-L147","doc":"**The 2×2 symplectic identity.** For any 2×2 matrix, `A · J₂ · Aᵀ = det A • J₂`\n— the dimension-2 fact behind `Sp₂ = SL₂`: contracting a bilinear form with a\n2×2 map scales it by the determinant. Direct entrywise computation\n(`det A = a·d − b·c`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.J2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.J2","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L135-L136","doc":"The standard 2×2 symplectic form `J₂ = [[0,-1],[1,0]]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.symplectic_det_sq_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.symplectic_det_sq_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L109-L126","doc":"**T1 — symplectic ⟹ `(det A)² = 1` (matrix-group infra).** A symplectic matrix\nsatisfies `A · J · Aᵀ = J`; taking determinants (`det J` is a unit,\n`isUnit_det_J`) gives `(det A)² = 1`. This is the matrix-group shadow of\n\"self-duality constrains the determinant\": in *every* dimension a\nsymplectic-form-preserving map has `det = ±1`. The refinement `det A = +1`\n(excluding `−1`), and thereby the `Sp₂ = SL₂` dim-2 accident, is the deeper\nconnectedness / Pfaffian fact — the base case of the classical residual T3,\ntracked in beans `qou-atsd-t1`/`t3`. Holds over any `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_subsingleton_of_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_subsingleton_of_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L91-L102","doc":"**Atomicity (PROVED, modulo T3 + T4).** Under the self-duality embedding, the\nclassical rank of the symplectic group, and the cohomological `dim V = 2`, the\nfundamental-object set `Fin (rank G)` is a subsingleton — **rank-one**. This is\nthe categorical-side conclusion the order-separation file assumes as\n`TensorGenerationFree`/totality; here it is *derived* from the volume-form\naxiom plus the two named classical residuals (`hRankSp` = T3; the connected-\nreductive input T4 is what guarantees `rank G` is the honest torus rank rather\nthan `0` for a finite subgroup — recorded, not needed for the `≤ 1` bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rankG_le_one_of_self_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rankG_le_one_of_self_dual","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L73-L89","doc":"**T2 — the rank collapse (PROVED, modulo the two named classical residuals).**\nGiven\n* `hEmbed : rankG ≤ rankSp dimV` — the self-duality embedding `G ⊆ Sp(V)`\n  (a symplectic-form-preserving subgroup has rank at most that of `Sp(V)`),\n* `hRankSp : ∀ m, rankSp (2*m) = m` — the classical fact `rank Sp(2m) = m`\n  (**T3**; the `m = 1` case is the `Sp₂ = SL₂` dim-2 accident), and\n* `hDim : dimV = 2` — the cohomological input (`dim V = rank H¹(Bring) = 2`),\n\nthe Tannaka dual has `rankG ≤ 1`. This is the arithmetic heart of the atomicity\nderivation; `hRankSp` is an explicit **hypothesis**, never an instance — the\nhonest open residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.subsingleton_fin_of_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.subsingleton_fin_of_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L67-L71","doc":"**Subsingleton from a rank bound.** `Fin (rank G)` — the set of fundamental\nobjects, indexed by `rank G` fundamental weights — is a subsingleton (`≤ 1`\nelement) exactly when `rank G ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.dim_two_of_choose_two_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.dim_two_of_choose_two_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityFromSelfDuality.lean#L49-L63","doc":"**T0 — the dimension-two crux.** The categorical determinant\n`ε : Λ²V → 𝟙` being an isomorphism onto the tensor unit means `Λ²V` is\n1-dimensional, i.e. `binom(dim V, 2) = 1`; the only natural number with\n`binom(n, 2) = 1` is `n = 2`. So a non-degenerate volume form on `V` of the\nshape `V ⊗ V → 𝟙` (a *bilinear* determinant) forces `dim V = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}